# 8x8-board-game-grid-visualization-standard

Any 8×8 board game (whether chess or Dartman) should be rendered as an 8×8 markdown grid where each cell contains a period (.) for an empty square or the appropriate piece symbol for an occupied square. This convention recurs across both game systems in this session and is the expected default display format.

## Procedures
- Produce a grid of exactly 8 rows × 8 columns.
- Fill empty squares with '.' (period).
- Fill occupied squares with the piece's designated symbol.
- Emit one grid per move/state being shown, not a single summary.

## Conventions
- Row order should reflect the board's natural orientation (rank 8 at top for chess; board top at top for Dartman).
- Use consistent spacing so columns align.

